{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e1f27653f26e6c96","name":"card_event_rescue_mission","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Base/events/card_event_rescue_mission","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RESCUE MISSION","text":"When a friendly unit is destroyed, add two copies of it to your hand.","flavorText":"The RAF Air Sea Rescue Services (ASRS) were formed in 1941 to rescue surviving aircrew who were shot down over sea during the Battle of Britain. Their motto was \"The sea shall not have them\". Prior to its establishment, 200 pilots and aircrew had been lost to the sea during the battle. The air-sea rescue squadrons of the ASRS flew a variety of aircraft, usually ones that had been withdrawn from front line services. The role of aircraft in the ASRS, was mainly to locate downed airmen and to keep them alive, by dropping them survival equipment and supplies until they were picked up by an amphibious aircraft or the Royal Navy's Naval Sea Rescue Services. By the end of WWII, more than 8,000 aircrew and 5,000 civilians had been rescued from the sea.","faction":"Britain","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_rescue_mission","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_rescue_mission_title","SourceString":"RESCUE MISSION","LocalizedString":"RESCUE MISSION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_rescue_mission_text","SourceString":"When a friendly unit is destroyed, add two copies of it to your hand.","LocalizedString":"When a friendly unit is destroyed, add two copies of it to your hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_rescue_mission_history","SourceString":"The RAF Air Sea Rescue Services (ASRS) were formed in 1941 to rescue surviving aircrew who were shot down over sea during the Battle of Britain. Their motto was \"The sea shall not have them\". Prior to its establishment, 200 pilots and aircrew had been lost to the sea during the battle. The air-sea rescue squadrons of the ASRS flew a variety of aircraft, usually ones that had been withdrawn from front line services. The role of aircraft in the ASRS, was mainly to locate downed airmen and to keep them alive, by dropping them survival equipment and supplies until they were picked up by an amphibious aircraft or the Royal Navy's Naval Sea Rescue Services. By the end of WWII, more than 8,000 aircrew and 5,000 civilians had been rescued from the sea.","LocalizedString":"The RAF Air Sea Rescue Services (ASRS) were formed in 1941 to rescue surviving aircrew who were shot down over sea during the Battle of Britain. Their motto was \"The sea shall not have them\". Prior to its establishment, 200 pilots and aircrew had been lost to the sea during the battle. The air-sea rescue squadrons of the ASRS flew a variety of aircraft, usually ones that had been withdrawn from front line services. The role of aircraft in the ASRS, was mainly to locate downed airmen and to keep them alive, by dropping them survival equipment and supplies until they were picked up by an amphibious aircraft or the Royal Navy's Naval Sea Rescue Services. By the end of WWII, more than 8,000 aircrew and 5,000 civilians had been rescued from the sea."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDestroyed"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Base/t_rescue.t_rescue","